 on the serial"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"executor of this actor."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If that is the case, the operation is invoked with an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isolated"},{"type":"text","text":" version"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of the actor, allowing synchronous access to actor local state without"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"hopping through asynchronous boundaries."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If the current context is not running on the actor’s serial executor, or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"if the actor is a reference to a remote actor, this method will crash"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with a fatal error (similar to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"preconditionIsolated()"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Note that this check is performed against the passed in actor’s serial"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"executor, meaning that if another actor uses the same serial executor–by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"using that actor’s "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Actor\/unownedExecutor","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" as its own"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Actor\/unownedExecutor","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"–this check will succeed, as from a concurrency"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"safety perspective, the serial executor guarantees mutual exclusion of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"those two actors."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This method can only be used from synchronous functions, as asynchronous"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"typ